(664371, 68739, 2333, '<td valign="top">great subject! Good use of negative space. I''d have been sorely tempted to clone out the wires, LOL. Guess there was nothing you could really do to eliminate them.<br/>I think my only serious suggestions would be to increase contrast and sharpen slightly more post-resizing to bring out some of the interesting texture in the coach &amp; field, and also to try for more contrast in the sky; the sky contrast might be enhanced by creative use of channel mixing during grey conversion, or a polarizer might have brought out more contrast in the original shot.</td>', 'great subject! Good use of negative space. I''d have been sorely tempted to clone out the wires, LOL. Guess there was nothing you could really do to eliminate them.I think my only serious suggestions would be to increase contrast and sharpen slightly more post-resizing to bring out some of the interesting texture in the coach & field, and also to try for more contrast in the sky; the sky contrast might be enhanced by creative use of channel mixing during grey conversion, or a polarizer might have brought out more contrast in the original shot.', '2004-04-12 18:48:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(664373, 68150, 5213, '<td valign="top">This is OK, but I would have turned the wheel over so the logo is upright.</td>', 'This is OK, but I would have turned the wheel over so the logo is upright.', '2004-04-12 18:49:19.000000', NULL, 1),
