(666804, 68679, 2700, '<td valign="top">stunning... i didn''t vote on this, but amazing work. <br/>I think it acheives much shock as the voter is saying "wtf is that, how is it a wheel" takes a sec, but you see it in the end... VERY creative<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-14 01:08:46.</i></td>', 'stunning... i didn''t vote on this, but amazing work. I think it acheives much shock as the voter is saying "wtf is that, how is it a wheel" takes a sec, but you see it in the end... VERY creative', '2004-04-14 02:08:24.000000', '2004-04-14 02:08:46.000000', 0),
(666833, 68595, 16591, '<td valign="top">First of all, i would like to thank everyone for comments, really appreciate.<br/> <br/>Some of you would like to know how i did this.<br/> <br/>First step, how to stay the wheel standing instead of lying down, use anything small which is able to hide from the capture scene, here I use paper rolled up and placed it under. <br/> <br/>Set your camera ready with self-timer. <br/> <br/>How to make smoke, simple - light a cigarette then place it under the wheel but touching nothing. You do not want to mess up the platform with ashes or tip the wheel over. Place the cigarette there for quite a while to accumulate the smoke.  When you think it is ready to go, push the shutter and notice the countdown.  Hide the cigarette before the cameras take the shot. <br/> <br/>And of course some lighting will help, I use one table lamp on top and two spotlights on both side, left and right. <br/> <br/>For options review please go to <a href="//www.deviantart.com/view/6378162/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.deviantart.com/view/6378162/</a> <br/></td>', 'First of all, i would like to thank everyone for comments, really appreciate. Some of you would like to know how i did this. First step, how to stay the wheel standing instead of lying down, use anything small which is able to hide from the capture scene, here I use paper rolled up and placed it under.  Set your camera ready with self-timer.  How to make smoke, simple - light a cigarette then place it under the wheel but touching nothing. You do not want to mess up the platform with ashes or tip the wheel over. Place the cigarette there for quite a while to accumulate the smoke.  When you think it is ready to go, push the shutter and notice the countdown.  Hide the cigarette before the cameras take the shot.  And of course some lighting will help, I use one table lamp on top and two spotlights on both side, left and right.  For options review please go to //www.deviantart.com/view/6378162/ ', '2004-04-14 02:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(666864, 68679, 16907, '<td valign="top">I must say, I''m a bit disappointed - just 8 ones?!<br/>I was expecting at least 29 (same as tens) :))<br/> <br/>Thanks for the pile of comments :), I guess not everybody in this challenge was that open minded after all.<br/> <br/>This one was really fun! At least I''m heading for my most commented photo :))</td>', 'I must say, I''m a bit disappointed - just 8 ones?!I was expecting at least 29 (same as tens) :)) Thanks for the pile of comments :), I guess not everybody in this challenge was that open minded after all. This one was really fun! At least I''m heading for my most commented photo :))', '2004-04-14 02:56:22.000000', NULL, 0),
