(667029, 68194, 16004, '<td valign="top">There is such an unbalanced level of justice in this world - how on earth did you achieve 17 tens AND 17 ones (BTW, i''m on the side of those giving the tens)?  I feel quite aggrieved on your account here, as this deserved to do far better than 72nd.  I think I shall stage a protest outside the houses of parliament, so we can invade the DPC headquarters and sort out this (and i don''t use the word lightly) TRAVESTY of justice.  <br/> <br/>PS, nice one and keep up the good work!</td>', 'There is such an unbalanced level of justice in this world - how on earth did you achieve 17 tens AND 17 ones (BTW, i''m on the side of those giving the tens)?  I feel quite aggrieved on your account here, as this deserved to do far better than 72nd.  I think I shall stage a protest outside the houses of parliament, so we can invade the DPC headquarters and sort out this (and i don''t use the word lightly) TRAVESTY of justice.   PS, nice one and keep up the good work!', '2004-04-14 05:30:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(667032, 68625, 18897, '<td valign="top">Can''t believe you''re down at 36 with this one. Perhaps you were penalized for having tires and not wheels, but I think they qualify well. You received my only 10 this round and I hoped you''d get up a lot higher. I just love it!</td>', 'Can''t believe you''re down at 36 with this one. Perhaps you were penalized for having tires and not wheels, but I think they qualify well. You received my only 10 this round and I hoped you''d get up a lot higher. I just love it!', '2004-04-14 05:34:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(667035, 68385, 18960, '<td valign="top">I wonder if it is "compositionally perfect?" The rule of thirds is an empirical determination to attempt an explanation of why we respond so favorably to one image and perhaps not to another. One of the things we seem not to enjoy so much is an image divided in half, and your picture seems to be, diagonally. The geometrical average of the mass of the wonderful little girl fills in just exactly half the shot. So maybe that is part of people''s reaction. Maybe it is cropped too tight.<br/> <br/>Also, your fill-in flash is perhaps a bit overdone. The face is featureless, the eyebrows are missing and the image in right on the edge of being blown out.</td>', 'I wonder if it is "compositionally perfect?" The rule of thirds is an empirical determination to attempt an explanation of why we respond so favorably to one image and perhaps not to another. One of the things we seem not to enjoy so much is an image divided in half, and your picture seems to be, diagonally. The geometrical average of the mass of the wonderful little girl fills in just exactly half the shot. So maybe that is part of people''s reaction. Maybe it is cropped too tight. Also, your fill-in flash is perhaps a bit overdone. The face is featureless, the eyebrows are missing and the image in right on the edge of being blown out.', '2004-04-14 05:37:18.000000', NULL, 0),
