(667253, 68150, 16430, '<td valign="top">This shot showed me how hard it is to shoot chrome, without the tripod, camera and myself showing in the surface. After many failures, I finally held up a dark cloth between myself and the camera to mask the  reflections. Also, a comment was made about the logo being upside down, which I was well aware of, but rotating the wheel showed the valve stem and that looked more distracting than the logo. Anyway, I am quite pleased that it rated this high and really appreciate all the great comments and votes.</td>', 'This shot showed me how hard it is to shoot chrome, without the tripod, camera and myself showing in the surface. After many failures, I finally held up a dark cloth between myself and the camera to mask the  reflections. Also, a comment was made about the logo being upside down, which I was well aware of, but rotating the wheel showed the valve stem and that looked more distracting than the logo. Anyway, I am quite pleased that it rated this high and really appreciate all the great comments and votes.', '2004-04-14 08:25:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(667263, 68761, 14603, '<td valign="top">I suffered similarly when I tried a technique similar to this in the "Portrait" challenge.<br/> <br/>Don`t worry about it keep experimenting.<br/> <br/>Gordon</td>', 'I suffered similarly when I tried a technique similar to this in the "Portrait" challenge. Don`t worry about it keep experimenting. Gordon', '2004-04-14 08:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(667266, 68152, 16636, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, I was very pleased with the outcome of this image. I added the sepia and noise to the image to bring a historical feel to the image - well it is the University back streets in Oxford.<br/>Thanks again.....</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, I was very pleased with the outcome of this image. I added the sepia and noise to the image to bring a historical feel to the image - well it is the University back streets in Oxford.Thanks again.....', '2004-04-14 08:32:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(667370, 68385, 14255, '<td valign="top">I gave this shot a 3. My reason being that I didn''t feel that it met the challenge which was to take a shot of " a Wheel ". It''s a lovely shot of your daughter but I felt that the bike in the background was secondary to the main subject which was your daughter.<br/>I feel that i scored your shot fairly.  One of my favourite shots from this challenge was of flowers (I commented on that shot that I would have happily given it a 10 if the challenge was to take a shot of some flowers but as it didn''t meet the challenge I gave it a 1)<br/></td>', 'I gave this shot a 3. My reason being that I didn''t feel that it met the challenge which was to take a shot of " a Wheel ". It''s a lovely shot of your daughter but I felt that the bike in the background was secondary to the main subject which was your daughter.I feel that i scored your shot fairly.  One of my favourite shots from this challenge was of flowers (I commented on that shot that I would have happily given it a 10 if the challenge was to take a shot of some flowers but as it didn''t meet the challenge I gave it a 1)', '2004-04-14 09:31:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(667378, 68679, 14255, '<td valign="top">As hard as I try still can''t make out what this is or how it is a wheel</td>', 'As hard as I try still can''t make out what this is or how it is a wheel', '2004-04-14 09:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(667379, 68700, 17745, '<td valign="top">So here it was, one day before the deadline and I had nothing.  Going through my garage, I came across an old pair of rollerblades.  Decided to pull the wheels off to see what they looked like off the skate and proceeded to setup a couple of shots.  An hour into shooting, my wife popped in to see how it was going and suggested I set up a shot where the wheels spelled "TRUE".  I had been trying to figure out what the letters stood for during the first hour of shooting, but with being under the gun it just wasn''t coming to me.  <br/> <br/>A couple of shots later it was off to PS for some adjustments, then a quick run through Neat Image.  This was the final product.  Though the wheels had some scratches on them, especially on some of the white lettering, I was rather satisfied with it.  <br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone that liked and voted for it.  Being rather new to the site and this only being my 3 challenge, I was very happy with the 14th place it took.  Congratulations to the ribbon winners and everyone for that manner for a job well done!!       <br/></td>', 'So here it was, one day before the deadline and I had nothing.  Going through my garage, I came across an old pair of rollerblades.  Decided to pull the wheels off to see what they looked like off the skate and proceeded to setup a couple of shots.  An hour into shooting, my wife popped in to see how it was going and suggested I set up a shot where the wheels spelled "TRUE".  I had been trying to figure out what the letters stood for during the first hour of shooting, but with being under the gun it just wasn''t coming to me.   A couple of shots later it was off to PS for some adjustments, then a quick run through Neat Image.  This was the final product.  Though the wheels had some scratches on them, especially on some of the white lettering, I was rather satisfied with it.   Thanks to everyone that liked and voted for it.  Being rather new to the site and this only being my 3 challenge, I was very happy with the 14th place it took.  Congratulations to the ribbon winners and everyone for that manner for a job well done!!       ', '2004-04-14 09:39:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(667381, 67911, 18914, '<td valign="top"><br/>Hand held!! awesome shot!</td>', 'Hand held!! awesome shot!', '2004-04-14 09:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
