(667812, 68615, 4090, '<td valign="top">Many Thanks to everyone who voted on this - The funny thing is I wasn''t going to enter this as I wasn''t 100% happy. That is me sitting on the bench on the right. use the canon 70-200 F4 L Lens zoomed in at 200mm - Really happy that people like this photo. Regards Tony</td>', 'Many Thanks to everyone who voted on this - The funny thing is I wasn''t going to enter this as I wasn''t 100% happy. That is me sitting on the bench on the right. use the canon 70-200 F4 L Lens zoomed in at 200mm - Really happy that people like this photo. Regards Tony', '2004-04-14 13:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(667857, 68686, 18868, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who commented.  This image really seemed to polarize folks.  My general sense is that people either liked or hated the lighting.  I was attempting to get "dramatic" light on the slightly pebbled surface of the wall, but in retrospect, I think it was just dark and blah.  If I were to do it again, I would place a white card on the left side to fill in a little and even out the background.  <br/> <br/>And, of course, in the days after the contest ended, I figured out several better ways of hanging the model.  I had rushed into it, and it was a bit of a last minute deal... I hoped that the creativity of the idea would raise the score.<br/> <br/>This is one of those cases in which I liked it a lot when I submitted it, but don''t like it as well now.</td>', 'Thanks to all who commented.  This image really seemed to polarize folks.  My general sense is that people either liked or hated the lighting.  I was attempting to get "dramatic" light on the slightly pebbled surface of the wall, but in retrospect, I think it was just dark and blah.  If I were to do it again, I would place a white card on the left side to fill in a little and even out the background.   And, of course, in the days after the contest ended, I figured out several better ways of hanging the model.  I had rushed into it, and it was a bit of a last minute deal... I hoped that the creativity of the idea would raise the score. This is one of those cases in which I liked it a lot when I submitted it, but don''t like it as well now.', '2004-04-14 13:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(667966, 68668, 16912, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the votes peeps, my highest score to date and plenty of room for improvement :) oh, and look no 1''s and only 1x2. I guess I should reshoot this with all your advice taken into account.</td>', 'Thanks for all the votes peeps, my highest score to date and plenty of room for improvement :) oh, and look no 1''s and only 1x2. I guess I should reshoot this with all your advice taken into account.', '2004-04-14 14:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(668066, 68194, 11467, '<td valign="top">Sorry you didn''t do better. I was expecting this to be the winner!! Was my top placer.<br/>I think there must be too many people here without imagination. (Or humor).<br/>Keep up the good work. I had a great laugh with this, and also thought the photograph was great.</td>', 'Sorry you didn''t do better. I was expecting this to be the winner!! Was my top placer.I think there must be too many people here without imagination. (Or humor).Keep up the good work. I had a great laugh with this, and also thought the photograph was great.', '2004-04-14 14:42:50.000000', NULL, 0),
