(676759, 68441, 12253, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Impressions: I like the concept, and the shot of the tires with great DOF works well.  I particularly like that we get a closeup of a tire in the foreground which looks like it has pretty uneven tire wear.<br/> <br/>Improvements: Looks like your camera failed you a bit, as there appears to be purple fringing around the trees.  The sky itself seems a bit odd in color as well.  Compositionally, it might have been better to use a vertical division into thirds, e.g., two thirds tires, one third sky (or vice versa, but since the tires are the subject, I think two-thirds tires.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: Impressions: I like the concept, and the shot of the tires with great DOF works well.  I particularly like that we get a closeup of a tire in the foreground which looks like it has pretty uneven tire wear. Improvements: Looks like your camera failed you a bit, as there appears to be purple fringing around the trees.  The sky itself seems a bit odd in color as well.  Compositionally, it might have been better to use a vertical division into thirds, e.g., two thirds tires, one third sky (or vice versa, but since the tires are the subject, I think two-thirds tires. ', '2004-04-20 01:17:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(676921, 68615, 16672, '<td valign="top">How were you able to get the depth of field on the wheel thing while not getting the back image since you obviously had your aperture set pretty small to get the clarity you received in the reflected image?</td>', 'How were you able to get the depth of field on the wheel thing while not getting the back image since you obviously had your aperture set pretty small to get the clarity you received in the reflected image?', '2004-04-20 05:16:50.000000', NULL, 0),
