(1063754, 68615, 27845, '<td valign="top">I appreciate how you managed not to be too visible in the reflection. You did this <i>handheld?</i> Wow. My pictures turn shake if a use triple zoom without a tripod...</td>', 'I appreciate how you managed not to be too visible in the reflection. You did this handheld? Wow. My pictures turn shake if a use triple zoom without a tripod...', '2004-12-15 09:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1100802, 68686, 9932, '<td valign="top">I really like this idea and shot.<br/>I think it would have been so much better with even lighting on the background. Very nice idea.</td>', 'I really like this idea and shot.I think it would have been so much better with even lighting on the background. Very nice idea.', '2005-01-10 23:13:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1123236, 68027, 10634, '<td valign="top">Just wanted to reply to the "Crop" comments... I didn''t crop it. I wanted as close a shot of the tire as possible and to get the detail I was looking for, this was as much of the truck as I could get in the shot. Had I moved slightly to the right, there would be a complete rear tire, but still no top of the truck because the front tire (and main subject) is at the bottom of the frame. Then the crop would have been altogether too tight.<br/> <br/>Jen<br/> <br/>P.S.  Thank you everyone for taking the time to comment!</td>', 'Just wanted to reply to the "Crop" comments... I didn''t crop it. I wanted as close a shot of the tire as possible and to get the detail I was looking for, this was as much of the truck as I could get in the shot. Had I moved slightly to the right, there would be a complete rear tire, but still no top of the truck because the front tire (and main subject) is at the bottom of the frame. Then the crop would have been altogether too tight. Jen P.S.  Thank you everyone for taking the time to comment!', '2005-01-21 11:55:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1335748, 68668, 34986, '<td valign="top">I like this shot does look a little busy</td>', 'I like this shot does look a little busy', '2005-04-27 23:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
